{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Extract build_model_settings() and build_usage_limits()\n\nADR 0056 decision 3, SECOND extraction. Sequenced after the except-spine extraction because both edit\nrun(); there is no logical dependency between them.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/runner.py ~384-463 -> two plain functions with EXPLICIT parameters:\n      build_model_settings(cfg, req, caps, resolved, *, model_override) -> dict\n      build_usage_limits(cfg, req, UsageLimits) -> tuple\n  covering max_tokens, timeout, temperature (incl. the withdrawal matrix), max_iterations and the\n  per-run request ceiling.\n- tests/unit/\n\n## Explicitly NOT a frozen carrier object\n\nADR 0056 rejects the `ResolvedCall` dataclass an earlier draft proposed. Two of its seven fields\n(model_settings, provenance) are mutated after construction -- task cc33 writes\nprovider_provenance[\"ran_model\"] AFTER the finally block -- so the freeze would be decorative exactly\nwhere it matters, at a cost of ~30-40 lines of replace() ceremony to relocate ~113 lines of code. Use\nexplicit parameters; introduce a carrier only if a signature exceeds ~6 parameters.\n\n## Honest accounting\n\nThis region is 50% comment: ~80 lines is ~36 lines of executable code. The comments TRAVEL WITH the\ncode -- they are the temperature-deprecation matrix and the per-request-vs-config precedence\nrationale, and they are the reason the region is readable at all. Do not strip them to hit a number.\nPer AGENTS.md, do not create a module under 100 LOC by splitting: group these into ONE themed module\nrather than a file per function.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier, no network -- pure given cfg/req/caps.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a test asserts temperature is WITHDRAWN for a caps record with supports_temperature False and\n      RETAINED when True -- the negative control is what stops a \"withdraw always\" implementation passing\n- [ ] a test asserts a per-request output cap can only RAISE the configured floor, never lower it\n- [ ] a test asserts a per-request step budget likewise only raises\n- [ ] the extracted module is at or above the 100-LOC anti-fragmentation floor\n- [ ] any monkeypatch target that moved is repointed IN THE SAME COMMIT and named in the message\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785511855858433001,"uuid":"4d0787e9-e6d1-4d47-91c2-c6066778c445"}